//! Polling surface for async tasks (`Poll<T>`).
//!
//! ## Overview
//!
//! `std.core.future` defines the minimal contract for Arandu coroutines and
//! async tasks. It exposes `Poll<T>` — the result of a single poll step — and
//! `Context`, the execution token passed by the executor.
//!
//! The full `Future` interface (with `poll`) and `Waker` integration build on
//! top of this. The cooperative executor lives in `std.runtime.executor`.
//!
//! `Poll<T>` has two variants:
//! - `Poll.Ready(T)` — the task finished with value `T`
//! - `Poll.Pending` — the task is not done; the executor must reschedule
//!
//! ## Example
//!
//! ```arandu
//! import std.core.future as future
//!
//! func pollStep(): future.Poll<i32> {
//!     // remaining work:
//!     return future.Poll.Pending
//! }
//! ```
//!
//! ## Platform
//! `native` · `wasm32`
//!
//! wasm32 runs a single-threaded executor. On bare-metal only `Poll<T>` is
//! available — there is no executor.
//!
//! ## See also
//!
//! - `std.runtime.executor` — cooperative async task executor
//! - `std.runtime.waker` — `Waker` and `Context` (experimental)

module std.core.future

/// Result of one poll step on a coroutine / future.
public enum Poll<T> {
    /// The asynchronous value is available.
    Ready(T)
    /// The asynchronous operation has not completed.
    Pending
}

/// Execution context passed to an asynchronous task's poll step.
public struct Context {
    /// Opaque pointer to the runtime waker handle.
    waker: ptr[void]?
}

/// A value that can be asynchronously polled to completion.
public interface Future<T> {
    /// Attempts to resolve the future to a final value.
    func poll(self: mut ref Self, ctx: mut ref Context): Poll<T>
}

